# aws-cdk-lib resolves esbuild from its own location to decide whether it can
# bundle locally. Under pnpm's strict node_modules it can't see our esbuild, so
# it silently falls back to Docker bundling - where pnpm's symlinked deps don't
# resolve at all and every Lambda fails with "Could not resolve <package>".
# Hoisting esbuild keeps bundling local, which is also much faster.
#
# This hoists whichever esbuild pnpm's algorithm picks, so it is only safe
# while the tree holds exactly one version. The root pnpm.overrides entry for
# esbuild is what guarantees that; without it a transitive bump elsewhere can
# flip which version gets hoisted and break synth again. Keep the two in step.
public-hoist-pattern[]=esbuild
